<title>FINLAND: ICE HOCKEY-WORLD CHAMPIONSHIP RESULTS.</title>
<headline>ICE HOCKEY-WORLD CHAMPIONSHIP RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>TURKU, Finland 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results at the world ice</p>
<p>hockey championships on Monday:</p>
<p>Pool B</p>
<p>Italy 5 Latvia 4 (0-1 2-3 3-0)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Latvia - Leonids Tambijevs (8:17), Andrei Maticins (28:03),</p>
<p>Harius Vitolins (28:18), Aleksandrs Macijevskis (29:40)</p>
<p>Italy - Leo Giuseppe Insam (25:38), Gaetano Orlando (33:07),</p>
<p>Mario Chitarroni (42:08), Bruno Zarrillo (45:38, 49:37)</p>
<p>Penalties: Italy 20 minutes, Latvia 14</p>
<p>Attendance: 3,506</p>
<p>Pool A (In Helsinki):</p>
<p>Germany 1 Russia 5 (0-0 1-2 0-3)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Germany - Bradley Bergen (31:38).</p>
<p>Russia - Oleg Belov (25:09), Sergei Petrenko (32:14),</p>
<p>Anatoly Fedotov (47:19), Mikhail Sarmatin (59:39), Alexei</p>
<p>Morozov (59:58).</p>
<p>Penalties: Germany 10 minutes, Russia 12 minutes.</p>
<p>Attendance: 12,865.</p>
<p>Pool B</p>
<p>United States 3 Norway 1 (2-1 0-0 1-0)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>United States - Don Brashear (11:56), Ted Donato (19:14),</p>
<p>Michael Sullivan (59:04)</p>
<p>Norway - Svein Enok Norstebo (5:49)</p>
<p>Penalties: United States 16 minutes, Norway 12</p>
<p>Attendance: 3,450</p>
<p>Pool A (In Helsinki): Slovakia 5 France 3 (1-2 4-0 0-1)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Slovakia - Zdenko Ciger (07:21), Roman Stantien (22:35),</p>
<p>Roman Kontsek (24:44, 36:19), Jan Pardavy (25:56).</p>
<p>France - Brian Arnaud (03:13, 57:08), Cristian Pouget</p>
<p>(05:08).</p>
<p>Penalties: Slovakia 6 minutes, France 6 minutes.</p>
<p>Attendance: 12,911.</p>
</text>
